# 01_Raw_Data

## Overview

This directory contains the complete raw dataset acquired during the experimental evaluation described in the accompanying manuscript.

The data were collected directly from the MPU6050 inertial measurement unit (IMU) mounted on the ESP32-based embedded platform. These files represent the original measurements before any preprocessing, filtering, feature extraction, normalization, segmentation, or machine learning operations.

The purpose of providing the raw dataset is to ensure full transparency and reproducibility of the experimental workflow.

---

## Contents

This directory includes:

- Original sensor recordings
- Raw accelerometer measurements
- Raw gyroscope measurements
- Time stamps associated with each acquisition
- Original activity labels assigned during data collection (if available)
- Data acquisition notes

No modifications have been applied to these files.

---

## Data Description

The raw dataset contains measurements acquired directly from the MPU6050 sensor.

Typical recorded variables include:

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Timestamp | Sampling instant |
| Acc_X | X-axis acceleration |
| Acc_Y | Y-axis acceleration |
| Acc_Z | Z-axis acceleration |
| Gyro_X | X-axis angular velocity |
| Gyro_Y | Y-axis angular velocity |
| Gyro_Z | Z-axis angular velocity |
| Label | Motion class (when available) |

The exact variable names may vary depending on the acquisition software.

---

## Acquisition Procedure

The data acquisition process consisted of the following steps:

1. Initialization of the ESP32 embedded platform.
2. Configuration of the MPU6050 IMU.
3. Continuous acquisition of inertial measurements.
4. Storage of the acquired samples without preprocessing.
5. Export of the collected data in CSV format.

No filtering or feature engineering was performed during this stage.

---

## Data Integrity

The files contained in this directory are preserved exactly as acquired from the experimental platform.

Specifically, no:

- normalization,
- interpolation,
- missing-value correction,
- smoothing,
- window segmentation,
- feature extraction, or
- class balancing

has been applied.

All preprocessing operations are documented separately in the **02_Processed_Data** directory.

---

## Relationship to the Manuscript

These files constitute the starting point of the experimental workflow presented in the manuscript.

The workflow is summarized as follows:

```
Raw Data
    │
    ▼
Data Cleaning
    │
    ▼
Feature Extraction
    │
    ▼
Model Training
    │
    ▼
Embedded Deployment
```

The processed datasets generated from these files are available in:

```
02_Processed_Data/
```

---

## File Format

The raw data are provided in CSV format.

Encoding:

```
UTF-8
```

Delimiter:

```
Comma (,)
```

Decimal separator:

```
.
```

---

## Reproducibility

Researchers wishing to reproduce the experiments should begin with the files contained in this directory before performing any preprocessing or feature extraction.

These files represent the original experimental observations used throughout the study.

---

## Notes

The raw data are intentionally preserved without modification to maintain complete experimental traceability and facilitate independent verification of the reported results.
